{
  "_help": [
    "WordsForge - Bible Edition | content & translations file",
    "",
    "HOW TO ADD A LEVEL",
    "Each level is ONE line in the \"levels\" array, in this format:",
    "  [number, \"LETTERS\", \"MANDATORY\", \"WORD1,WORD2,WORD3\"]",
    "",
    "  number     - the level's display number (integer, just for labeling)",
    "  LETTERS    - every available letter for the level, no separators, e.g. \"ABCDEFG\"",
    "  MANDATORY  - one letter from LETTERS that every word must contain, or \"\" for none",
    "  WORDS      - comma-separated valid words (each 3+ letters, using only LETTERS)",
    "",
    "Example: [11, \"ABCDEFG\", \"C\", \"CAB,FACE,CAGE\"]",
    "",
    "HOW TO ADD/EDIT A LANGUAGE",
    "Copy a whole language block (e.g. \"en\": { ... }) and translate:",
    "  - \"name\"  : the language's display name shown in Settings",
    "  - \"menu\"  : every piece of UI text in the app (buttons, labels, messages)",
    "  - \"levels\": the level lines as described above, using that language's alphabet",
    "Then add your new language's key (e.g. \"fr\") next to \"en\", \"hy\", \"ru\" below,",
    "and it will show up automatically in Settings > General > Language.",
    "",
    "NOTE: the sample Armenian (hy) and Russian (ru) levels below are short",
    "placeholder examples to demonstrate the format - swap in your own",
    "Bible-themed word lists for each language."
  ],
